NetBSD src snapshot: 88b7858091c9fbc32bd7e475ea5a138a1a3b4819

BPF JIT source: sys/net/bpfjit.c and sys/net/bpfjit.h
Matching SLJIT source: sys/external/bsd/sljit/dist/sljit_src/
Both are from the same NetBSD src commit above.

The vendored NetBSD and SLJIT source files remain the pristine snapshot above.
All local adaptations are carried in patches/netbsd-bpfjit.patch and
patches/netbsd-sljit.patch and applied to copied sources in OUT_DIR; they are
not edits to the pristine upstream C files.

Those patches record the userspace adaptations: bpfjit.c selects libpcap's
pcap-bpf.h on Linux and the platform net/bpf.h elsewhere, includes this local
bpfjit.h, and only emits NetBSD RCSID macros on NetBSD. If sys/queue.h is
unavailable, it supplies only the SLIST macros used by bpfjit.c. bpfjit.h uses
bpf-compat.h to provide the private bpf_args_t/bpf_ctx_t ABI expected by this
crate. sljitConfig.h omits NetBSD's <machine/sljit_machdep.h>; build.rs supplies
automatic architecture selection and host-specific executable allocator
settings. The SLJIT tree's original per-file license notices and local LICENSE
are kept. Apple MAP_JIT and write-protection support is carried in the SLJIT
patch as executable allocator and ARM64 code-generation/patch-transition
adaptations.
